% A line of music with no note to sing, such as a line of rests, needs
% no lyrics, also in a voice that has lyrics on its other lines (GitHub
% issue #79).  checksyllables() (genmidi.c) looked for the lyrics of
% such a line from the start of the tune, did not find them and
% reported a "Line of music without lyrics", even with an empty w:
% field below the line.  In tune 1, voice A rests for two lines, the
% second one with an empty w: field.  Tune 2 has a single voice.
X:1
T:Lyrics and lines of rests in two voices
C:abc2midi test
M:C
L:1/4
Q:1/4=120
K:C
V:S
V:A
[V:S] C E G c |
w: do mi sol do
[V:A] z z z z |
[V:S] c G E C |
w: do sol mi do
[V:A] z4 |
w:
[V:S] C E G c |]
w: do mi sol do
[V:A] E G c e |]
w: mi sol do mi

X:2
T:Lyrics and a line of rests in one voice
C:abc2midi test
M:C
L:1/4
Q:1/4=120
K:C
C E G c |
w: do mi sol do
z4 |
c G E C |]
w: do sol mi do
